WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.440
A message arrives at the tip of an axon.

2
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.140
How does it get home?

3
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.500
One answer is a courier.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.020
A courier carries one parcel the whole way.

5
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.280
The other is a bucket brigade.

6
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.040
Each stretch of the axon hands the message to the next, and nothing physical makes

7
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.040
the whole journey.

8
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:27.603
The popular test is to block dynein, the motor.

9
00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:36.683
In 2004, Heerssen, Pazyra and Segal found that dynein motors transport activated Trk

10
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:42.323
receptors. They found that this transport is needed for the survival of neurons that

11
00:00:42.323 --> 00:00:43.483
depend on their target.

12
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:46.423
That is real evidence for a courier.

13
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:50.253
A brigade would fail the same test, though.

14
00:00:51.373 --> 00:00:56.453
Suppose each stretch of the axon needs dynein-driven transport for its own local

15
00:00:56.453 --> 00:01:02.473
step. Then blocking dynein stops the brigade as completely as it stops the courier.

16
00:01:02.953 --> 00:01:05.133
So the block cannot tell them apart.

17
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:08.703
The relay is a published alternative.

18
00:01:09.763 --> 00:01:15.903
In 2002, MacInnis and Campenot reported that retrograde signals can support neuron

19
00:01:15.903 --> 00:01:19.703
survival without retrograde transport of NGF itself.

20
00:01:21.043 --> 00:01:28.943
In 2003, Ye, Kuruvilla, Zweifel and Ginty titled their paper: Evidence in support of

21
00:01:28.943 --> 00:01:33.003
signaling endosome-based retrograde survival of sympathetic neurons.

22
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:35.703
The title claims support.

23
00:01:36.303 --> 00:01:37.683
It does not claim proof.

24
00:01:39.163 --> 00:01:44.403
Settled: NGF at the terminal is enough, a signal from the terminal reaches the

25
00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:48.983
nucleus, and dynein carries activated receptors that survival depends on.

26
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:53.643
Not settled: whether the carried receptor is the only route.
